+++ b/docs/requirements.rst
@@ -61,6 +61,23 @@ Usage
     >>> requirements1 == requirements2
     True
 
+Use ``__replace__`` to copy a requirement with selected fields changed. It
+accepts the keyword arguments ``name``, ``url``, ``extras``, ``specifier``, and
+``marker``, with the same types as the corresponding attributes. Unspecified
+fields are retained; invalid fields or combinations raise ``InvalidRequirement``.
+The original is unchanged, and specifier prerelease overrides are preserved
+without sharing mutable specifiers.
+
+.. doctest::
+
+    >>> req = Requirement('requests[security]>=2.0; python_version >= "3"')
+    >>> req.__replace__(name="flask")
+    <Requirement('flask[security]>=2.0; python_version >= "3"')>
+
+On Python 3.13 and later, ``copy.replace(req, name="flask")`` also works.
+Subclasses receive an instance of their own class, initialized from the new
+requirement string.
+
 .. versionchanged:: 23.2
 
